   "notes": "Global errors-in-variables inversion of 48 Guignot et al. static P-V-T observations and six PPv shock P-density states. V0=162.2 A^3 was fixed. Table 4 reports K0S=225(2) GPa, K0S'=4.21(7), theta0=990(146) K, gamma0=2.61(67), q=2.1(8), and Cvm=1.035(50) J g^-1 K^-1; Cvmax is the exact molar conversion using 100.3875 g mol^-1. The BM3 term is a 300 K reference isentrope, so thermal pressure subtracts energy at T_S(V)=Tr*theta(V)/theta0. The three source-reported shock temperatures are retained as measured diagnostics but are not constraints in the solid PPv inversion; section 3 explicitly identifies shock-temperature fitting only for MgSiO3 liquid.",
